@startuml fig-15-booking-sponsor-response
' =====================================================================
' Figure 15. Booking a slot yourself, and getting an answer from a person
' Type            : PlantUML-type, sequence diagram with activation bars
' Paper section   : § 6, Who Can Join, and Who Decides
' Concern answered: ChatGPT concern 16 (practical burdens) and the access half
'                   of concern 8 (treatment choice); Gemini family 1 (less time
'                   with the doctor). Under current practice a patient learns a
'                   trial exists from a clinician who happens to know about it,
'                   and every subsequent question routes back through that
'                   clinician. H. R. 9510 v5 proposes a direct channel. This
'                   figure draws what that channel does message by message, and
'                   what its service-level commitment is.
' Why this type   : Latency and ordering between five parties, with the point
'                   being who waits for whom. A sequence diagram with explicit
'                   activation bars is the only notation that shows blocking.
'
' TikZ: draw with the uml* vocabulary of patientstyle.sty.
' TikZ: Five lifelines at x = 0, 3.8, 7.6, 11.4, 15.2, headers as umlbox with
' TikZ:   text width 24mm at y = 0; mmlife dashed rules from y = -0.7 to -14.2.
' TikZ: umlact activation bars 2.6mm wide centred on each lifeline, spanning
' TikZ:   exactly the messages they enclose.
' TikZ: Messages are umlarrow solid for calls, umldash for returns, labels in
' TikZ:   \tiny\sffamily set ABOVE the arrow line, never on it.
' TikZ: Elapsed-time annotations sit in the right margin at x = 16.6 in
' TikZ:   \tiny\sffamily\itshape, right aligned, with a 0.3pt pagraym leader.
' TikZ: The one self-message on the Sponsor lifeline uses
' TikZ:   to[out=25,in=-25,looseness=6] on a 4mm loop.
' TikZ: The alt fragment is a protogray 0.5pt rectangle with an "alt" corner
' TikZ:   tab and a dashed divider between branches.
' =====================================================================

!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #00417A
skinparam ArrowFontColor #111111
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #6C757D
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #00417A
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #DCE8F1
skinparam ParticipantFontColor #111111
skinparam ActorBorderColor #00417A
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam SequenceGroupBorderColor #6C757D
skinparam SequenceGroupBackgroundColor #E9ECEF
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #E9ECEF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #6C757D

autonumber

actor "You" as PT
participant "Trial booking\nportal" as PORT
participant "Sponsor-Investigator\non call" as SI
participant "Site screening\ncoordinator" as SC
participant "Your treating\noncologist" as ONC

PT -> PORT : request a screening slot, 24/7, no referral required
activate PORT
PORT -> PORT : match against open cohorts and the sentinel window
PORT --> PT : provisional slot held for 72 hours
deactivate PORT

PT -> SI : ask a direct question about the device
activate SI
note right of SI #E9ECEF
  H. R. 9510 v5 proposes that this
  message reaches a named human at the
  sponsor, not a form, and that the
  answer is logged in your record.
end note
SI --> PT : answer, within one business day, recorded verbatim
deactivate SI

PT -> SC : confirm the slot
activate SC
SC -> ONC : request records and staging with your authorisation
activate ONC
ONC --> SC : imaging, pathology, KRAS G12 status
deactivate ONC
SC -> SC : eligibility pre-check against § 5.1 and § 5.2

alt eligible on paper
  SC --> PT : screening visit confirmed, itinerary and cost sheet attached
  SC -> ONC : notify, so your own care team is never bypassed
else not eligible on paper
  SC --> PT : reason stated in plain language, no record beyond the screening log
  SC -> ONC : notify, so your own care team can act on the reason
end
deactivate SC

note over PT, PORT #E9ECEF
  You never lose your treating oncologist. Every branch
  above notifies them. The channel is additional, not
  a replacement, which is the distinction the surveyed
  patients cared about most.
end note

note over SI, SC
  Elapsed time from first request to a confirmed
  screening visit, target: 5 business days.
  The 72-hour hold exists so you are not
  rushed into confirming.
end note

@enduml
